+### [2026-10-26] Changelog placement checks compare entry text
+
+**Context**: Guarding against entries that a clean merge files under a
+released version heading instead of `## [Unreleased]`.
+**Learning**: The guard in `scripts/update_changelog.py --check` compares the
+set of entry texts between the base revision and the head revision instead of
+diffing line positions. Entries that already existed in the base revision are
+accepted, so release rotation, rebases, merge commits, and link updates do not
+cause false positives.
+**Recommendation**: Keep the check content-based. Exempt release-generated
+content (the empty-release placeholder and comparison links) explicitly rather
+than skipping whole version sections, and run the check both on pull requests
+and on pushes to `dev`.
+
