+## Guarding changelog placement
+
+A release can rotate the pending `## [Unreleased]` entries into a version
+section while a pull request is still open.
+When that pull request merges, Git can apply its changelog hunk cleanly
+and file the new entry under the freshly released version
+instead of under `## [Unreleased]`.
+
+The `Changelog placement` workflow prevents that by running
+`scripts/update_changelog.py --check` on every pull request that touches
+`CHANGELOG.md`, and again on `dev` after each merge.
+The check compares entries by their text rather than by line position:
+
+- An entry is reported when it does not appear in the base revision
+  and is not filed under `## [Unreleased]`.
+- Entries that already existed in the base revision are accepted,
+  so the release rotation that moves them under a version heading passes.
+- Comparison link updates and the empty-release placeholder are ignored.
+- Because the comparison is content-based, rebases, merge commits,
+  and reordered entries do not produce false positives.
+
+To fix a failure, move the reported entry lines under `## [Unreleased]`
+and push again.
+If an entry was genuinely released in the version it is filed under,
+no change is needed once the base revision contains that entry.
+
